## Reproduction Steps

The issue author provided an excellent reproduction. I confirmed the root cause via code analysis.

### Setup

```bash
pnpm dlx create-mastra@latest mastra-bug-repro -c agents,tools -l google -n
cd mastra-bug-repro
pnpm add @ai-sdk/google @mastra/memory @mastra/libsql
```

### Reproduction Code

Create `src/repro.ts` (based on the issue author's code):

```ts
import { google } from "@ai-sdk/google";
import { Mastra } from "@mastra/core/mastra";
import { Agent } from "@mastra/core/agent";
import { createTool } from "@mastra/core/tools";
import { LibSQLStore } from "@mastra/libsql";
import { Memory } from "@mastra/memory";
import { z } from "zod";

const GEMINI_API_KEY = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY!;
const FILE_SEARCH_STORE = process.env.FILE_SEARCH_STORE!;

// Any second tool triggers the bug
const echoTool = createTool({
  id: "echo",
  description: "Echoes text. Do not call unless asked.",
  inputSchema: z.object({ text: z.string() }),
  execute: async ({ text }) => ({ echoed: text }),
});

const agent = new Agent({
  id: "chat",
  name: "Chat",
  instructions: "You are a helpful assistant. Use file_search for document questions.",
  model: { id: "google/gemini-3-flash-preview", apiKey: GEMINI_API_KEY },
  tools: {
    file_search: google.tools.fileSearch({ fileSearchStoreNames: [FILE_SEARCH_STORE] }),
    echo: echoTool,
  },
  memory: new Memory({
    options: {
      observationalMemory: { model: { id: "google/gemini-2.5-flash", apiKey: GEMINI_API_KEY } },
    },
  }),
});

const mastra = new Mastra({
  agents: { chat: agent },
  storage: new LibSQLStore({ id: "repro", url: "file:./repro.db" }),
});

async function turn(input: string, thread: string) {
  console.log(`\n=== USER: ${input} ===`);
  const s = await mastra.getAgent("chat").stream(input, {
    memory: { thread, resource: "u1" },
  });
  for await (const c of s.textStream) process.stdout.write(c);
  process.stdout.write("\n");
  if (s.error) throw s.error;
}

const thread = `repro-${Date.now()}`;
await turn("What documents do I have?", thread);
await turn("Tell me more about one of them.", thread);
```

### Run

```bash
# Create .env with GEMINI_API_KEY and FILE_SEARCH_STORE
GEMINI_API_KEY=<key> FILE_SEARCH_STORE=fileSearchStores/<your-store> npx tsx src/repro.ts
```

### Expected

Both turns succeed. file_search results are properly stored and replayed.

### Actual

Turn 1 logs warnings:
```
updateToolInvocation: no matching tool call found for toolCallId=<id>
```

Turn 2 fails:
```
AI_APICallError: contents[N].parts[0]: Corrupted tool call context.
status: 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT
```

### Root Cause (confirmed in source)

In `packages/core/src/agent/message-list/message-list.ts`, the `updateToolInvocation()` method (line 719-767) walks backwards through messages to find a matching tool-call by `toolCallId`. For `file_search` results, the `toolCallId` in the arriving result **does not match** the `toolCallId` of the stored tool-call. This causes:

1. The result is silently dropped (warning logged at line 766)
2. The stored tool-call never advances to `'result'` state
3. On the next turn, Gemini receives an incomplete tool-call context
4. Gemini rejects with `"Corrupted tool call context"`

Key observations from the issue author:
- Removing the second tool (echo) makes both turns succeed
- Reproduces on both `@mastra/libsql` and `@mastra/pg` (not storage-specific)
- First turn works, second turn fails (different from Google-side regressions)

