> Hi, I have a question. In your example, if const resourceId = `${tenantId}_${userId}`, how can we filter threads for a specific agent when making a request?

Hey @ginlink! I'm solving this by pushing the `agent` into the `metadata`, then filtering via the metadata:

```ts
return memory.listThreads({
    filter: { resourceId: `<resource-id>`, metadata: { agent } },
    page,
    perPage,
    orderBy: orderBy ? { field: 'createdAt', direction: orderBy } : undefined,
});
```

The call to `agent.stream()` adds that `metadata` manually:

```ts
memory: {
    thread: {
        id,
        metadata: {
            agent: <AGENT_NAME>,
        },
    },
}
```

Hope this helps!

The [BatchParts](https://mastra.ai/reference/processors/batch-parts-processor) processor is there to help with this kind of stuff. Another option for now if you don't want the processor to run on stream parts you can wrap the processor and only return the functions you want it to use.

```
class CustomModerationProcessor implement Processor {
  processInput(args) {
    return moderationProcessor.processInput(args)
  }
  ...
}
```

