We were able to fix this on our end. We had two problems:

(1) You need to pass your own braintrustLogger for it to check for an existing BT span:
``` 
new BraintrustExporter({
      braintrustLogger: initLogger({
        projectName: 'my agent name',
        apiKey: configuration.braintrust.apiKey,
      }),
    }),
```

(2) We needed to override the BT package version used by Mastra to be identical to ours. Otherwise each package version would get its own AsyncLocalStorage and Mastra would not see the span in the context created by our version.

@epinzur We made a initial attempt of this. Now the default exporter + playground would see scores on spans, and they are persistent for the default exporter as well. If this is the right direction, we will start implementing exporters logics (maybe langfuse first and then datadog once that gets merged?)

