Hi, I’m trying to implement semantic search within the resource scope but filtered by a specific metadata field.
My goal is to build a feature similar to ChatGPT’s “Projects” — essentially folders containing user conversations, where the agent can use messages from those threads as context.

According to the documentation, I currently create the threads while saving a projectId as metadata, for example:

```ts
stream(messages, {
  memory: {
    resource: "uid1",
    thread: {
      id: "tid1",
      metadata: { projectId }
    }  
  }
})
```

Would it be possible—just like with the “Metadata Filters” [mentioned in the RAG documentation](https://mastra.ai/en/reference/rag/metadata-filters) — to enable semantic recall that filters threads by this projectId, eg:

```ts
stream(messages, {
  memory: {
    ...
    options: {
      semanticRecall: {
        scope: 'resource',
        filter: {
          projectId: { $eq: projectId },
        }
      }
    }
  }
})
```

Would you recommend any other approach?

